# Hypervisor devices: virtio's NIC and disks; the NoCloud ISO, as a SCSI
# CD-ROM, for Lima; and the ACPI power button. Clouds' own devices are in
# prod.modules. And the root itself: erofs, on a loop device, through
# dm-verity, which stage0 mounts read-only in every form.
virtio_net virtio_blk sr_mod isofs evdev button erofs loop dm-verity
# The victim's filesystem bite leaves behind: ext4 (Debian, Ubuntu, and
# werewolf's own disk), xfs (Rocky), btrfs (Fedora). btrfs asks the crypto
# API for its checksum at mount time, after the loader is closed, so crc32c
# (its default, and Fedora's) is loaded here; xxhash64 and blake2b
# checksums would need xxhash_generic and blake2b_generic.
ext4 xfs btrfs crc32c-cryptoapi
# FAT, for werewolf's own disk (docs/design/native-boot.md): the updater and
# commit write the EFI partition. 437 and utf8 are FAT's default codepage
# and iocharset in Alpine's kernel.
vfat nls_cp437 nls_utf8
